# Do not auto-install peer dependencies.
#
# @solana/wallet-adapter-react depends on @solana-mobile/wallet-adapter-mobile,
# which declares `react-native: >0.74` as a non-optional peer. npm 7+ installs
# that peer automatically, which drags React Native and its bundler (metro) into
# a web app that never runs either — along with metro's `image-size`, which
# currently carries two unpatched high-severity denial-of-service advisories
# (vulnerable <=2.0.2; 2.0.2 is the latest release).
#
# Nothing here imports react-native. The mobile adapter only requires it from
# its `index.native.js` entry points, which metro selects and no web bundler
# ever resolves. So the peer is dead weight, and this drops it.
#
# The cost of this flag is that npm no longer validates peer ranges. Every peer
# this project actually needs — react, react-dom, next — is a direct dependency
# with an explicit version, and `npm run build` is the check that they agree.
legacy-peer-deps=true
